      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003, Elsevier Science (USA). All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Primitive neuroectodermal tumor (PNET) of the kidney is a rare entity with high malignant potential. Of the reported cases of renal PNET, patients presented with metastatic disease and had a poor response to therapy. The authors describe a rare case of an organ-confined primary PNET arising from the kidney in a 16-year-old girl who presented with vague abdominal pain. Tumor behavior and treatment modalities are discussed."
      },
